homelab-cert-server (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Dedicated fleet certificate issuer: certbot DNS-01 via
    homelab-api's narrow system_agent-gated _acme-challenge endpoint (so this
    host is never public-facing and cannot edit arbitrary DNS), plus
    homelab-cert-publish, which envelope-encrypts each renewed lineage and
    posts it to the certificate store. Publishing runs from certbot's
    deploy-hook AND from a timer that also drains a local spool -- certbot
    only WARNS on a failed hook, so without the timer an API blip during
    renewal would silently lose the publish for ~60 days.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:30:00 -0500
